{
  "name": "Counterspell",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You attempt to interrupt a creature in the process of casting a spell. The creature makes a Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the spell dissipates with no effect, and the action, Bonus Action, or Reaction used to cast it is wasted. If that spell was cast with a spell slot, the slot isn't expended.</p><p><em>Automation (midi-qol entries):</em> the whole of midi's Counterspell overlay written into the item, with overlays switched off for it, to edit as a homebrew item. Offered as your reaction when a creature you can see within 60 feet casts a spell with a Verbal, Somatic or Material component (the activity's use condition; midi raises the trigger for a cast, never for a leap, a chain's arc or a lingering area's turn). The caster makes the Constitution save; on a failure its spell fails and the slot it used isn't expended (the item's entry).</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
